--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/markdown/snippets/fortran_module_scanning.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+## Fortran module scanning follows gfortran
+
+The ninja backend's Fortran dependency scanner now reads sources the way
+gfortran does. Every module and submodule in a file is found, the `.smod`
+files of modules with separate module procedures are listed, continuation
+lines, `;`, fixed-form sources and `include` lines are understood, and sources
+that gfortran preprocesses are preprocessed with the target's `-D`, `-U` and
+`-I` arguments and gfortran's own `__GFORTRAN__` and `__GNUC__` macros before
+they are scanned. When several targets write a module file of the same name, a
+source depends on the one gfortran finds first on its module search path. When a
+file that a source includes changes, the sources are scanned again and the
+objects that include it are rebuilt.
